    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Foreword"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Well-being is not simply the absence of illness. It is a state of balance in which the body, the mind and the environment interact harmoniously. In our modern societies, many factors can compromise this balance: an unsuitable diet, lack of sleep, a sedentary lifestyle, chronic stress, mental overload or social isolation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Family Clinic approach rests on a holistic view of health. It holds that lasting well-being does not depend on a single solution but on combining several complementary pillars that act in synergy. A health-promoting diet, appropriate physical activity, restorative sleep, good emotional balance and a satisfying social life are the foundations of lasting health."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This booklet brings together the main lessons of the Family Clinic Well-Being collection and offers simple guideposts for gradually building a protective lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "What is well-being?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Well-being is a state in which a person feels able:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "To carry out their daily activities.",
        "To maintain their energy.",
        "To cope with life’s difficulties.",
        "To maintain satisfying relationships.",
        "To preserve their physical and mental health."
      ],
      "levels": [
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Well-being does not mean a life without constraints, but the ability to adapt to change while maintaining an overall balance."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "First pillar: a health-promoting diet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
