        "Excess refined sugars.",
        "Sugary drinks.",
        "Excess alcohol."
      ],
      "levels": [
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The goal is not perfection but the gradual improvement of eating habits."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Second pillar: restorative sleep"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sleep is one of the body’s most powerful natural recovery mechanisms."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "During the night:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "The brain reorganizes itself.",
        "Cells repair themselves.",
        "Hormones rebalance.",
        "The immune system grows stronger."
      ],
      "levels": [
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "To preserve sleep quality:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Keep regular hours.",
        "Cut back on screens in the evening.",
        "Avoid stimulants late in the day.",
        "Create a calm, dark environment."
      ],
      "levels": [
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Third pillar: physical activity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The human body is designed to move."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Regular physical activity helps to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Strengthen the cardiovascular system.",
        "Preserve the muscles.",
        "Maintain mobility.",
        "Reduce stress.",
        "Improve sleep.",
        "Promote healthy aging."
