    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Conclusion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lasting well-being rests on the balance of many interdependent factors. No single food, medication or method can guarantee good health on its own. On the other hand, combining a health-promoting diet, regular physical activity, restorative sleep, good stress management and a positive social environment makes it possible to gradually build up genuine health capital."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "According to the Family Clinic approach, every person has the means to improve their well-being through simple, realistic choices repeated every day. The path to better health begins with small actions, but their benefits can last a lifetime."
    }
